---
name: service
description: >-
  Create a JRebirth Service for slow, external, backend, or integration work
  (REST, DB gateway, file import/export, heavy computation). Use to keep long
  work out of Model, View, and Controller.
---
# Create Service

The Service handles work that is slow, external, or crosses a system boundary. It runs off the UI thread so the application stays responsive. Never put this kind of work in the Model, View, or Controller.

## Use when

The work is any of the following:

- A REST client call or HTTP request.
- A Spring backend bridge call or RPC.
- A file import or export operation.
- A report or document generation task.
- An expensive in-process computation.

## What does not belong in a Service

- Scene graph node building (belongs in the View).
- Trivial UI event handling (belongs in the Controller).
- Business orchestration that calls other commands in sequence (use a multi command instead).

## Key API

- Split into an interface and a `DefaultService` implementation registered with `@Register(value = FooService.class)`.
- Expose typed `WaveItem<T>` and `WaveType` constants on the interface for payload declaration.
- Name action methods `doXxx(payload, Wave)` so they bind to the wave pipeline automatically.
- Return results by sending a result wave. Never touch the scene graph directly from a Service.

Template: `templates/ServiceTemplate.java.txt`.
